theory.intro:
The direction of a nonzero vector is usually given as its **angle of inclination**, the angle turned anticlockwise from the positive $x$-axis, with $0^{\circ}\leq\theta<360^{\circ}$. Use degree mode. Sketch the vector; when both components are nonzero, find the reference angle $A=\tan^{-1}\frac{|y|}{|x|}$, then let the quadrant fix $\theta$. Handle axis directions directly; the zero vector has no direction.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.1]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (-2.4,1.8);
\coordinate (W) at (-3,0);
\coordinate (E) at (3,0);
\coordinate (F) at (-2.4,0);
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.8)--(0,2.8) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed] (P)--(F);
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(P) node[above right]{$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\pic[draw, "$A$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle = P--O--W};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=1.2cm, angle eccentricity=1.45] {angle = E--O--P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) The vector lies in the second quadrant. Use degree mode.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-7,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-1)--(0,6) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-6,5) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-6,5)--(-6,0);
\path (-3,0) node[below]{$6$} (-6,2.5) node[left]{$5$};
\draw[black] (-1.2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=140.1944,radius=6mm];
\path (-1.7,0.7) node{$A$};
\draw[->,draw={rgb,255:red,239;green,139;blue,44}] (1.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=140.1944,radius=9mm];
\path (1,2.1) node{$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{5}{6}\right)\\ A&\approx39.8056^{\circ}\\ \theta&=180^{\circ}-A\\ \theta&\approx140^{\circ}\end{align*}$
(b) The vector lies in the third quadrant.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-6,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-9)--(0,2) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-5,-8) node[below left]{$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-5,-8)--(-5,0);
\path (-2.5,0) node[above]{$5$} (-5,-4) node[left]{$8$};
\draw[black] (-1.2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=237.9946,radius=6mm];
\path (-1.7,-0.8) node{$A$};
\draw[->,draw={rgb,255:red,239;green,139;blue,44}] (1.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=237.9946,radius=9mm];
\path (0.8,2.1) node{$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{8}{5}\right)\\ A&\approx57.9946^{\circ}\\ \theta&=180^{\circ}+A\\ \theta&\approx238^{\circ}\end{align*}$

(a) Both components are positive, so the vector lies in the first quadrant.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-0.5,0)--(4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.5)--(0,2.5) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(3.4641,2) node[above]{$\underset{\sim}{p}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (3.4641,2)--(3.4641,0);
\path (1.732,0) node[below]{$3\sqrt{3}$} (3.4641,1) node[right]{$3$};
\draw[black] (1,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=30,radius=8mm];
\path (1.4,0.4) node{$A=\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{3\sqrt{3}}\right)\\ A&=30^{\circ}\\ \theta&=30^{\circ}\end{align*}$
(b) The vector lies in the fourth quadrant.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-0.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3.5)--(0,2) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(3,-3) node[below right]{$\underset{\sim}{q}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (3,-3)--(3,0);
\path (1.5,0) node[above]{$4$} (3,-1.5) node[right]{$4$};
\draw[black] (1,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-45,radius=8mm];
\path (1.4,-0.5) node{$A$};
\draw[->,draw={rgb,255:red,239;green,139;blue,44}] (1.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=315,radius=12.8mm];
\path (-1.2,1.2) node{$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{4}{4}\right)\\ A&=45^{\circ}\\ \theta&=360^{\circ}-45^{\circ}\\ \theta&=315^{\circ}\end{align*}$

The displacement lies in the second quadrant. A true bearing is measured clockwise from north.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-13,0)--(3,0) node[right]{$E$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-2)--(0,7) node[above]{$N$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-12,5) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{s}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-12,5)--(-12,0);
\path (-6,0) node[below]{$12$} (-12,2.5) node[left]{$5$};
\draw[black] (-2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=157.3801,radius=8mm];
\path (-3,0.8) node{$A$};
\draw[->,draw={rgb,255:red,239;green,139;blue,44}] (0,3.5) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-202.6199,radius=14mm];
\path (4,-3) node{bearing};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{5}{12}\right)\\ A&\approx22.6199^{\circ}\\ \theta&=180^{\circ}-A\\ \theta&\approx157.3801^{\circ}\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}\text{bearing}&=90^{\circ}-\theta+360^{\circ}\\ \text{bearing}&\approx292.6199^{\circ}\\ \text{bearing}&\approx293^{\circ}\text{T}\end{align*}$

(a) Add corresponding components.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}\\ &= (2-6)\mathbf{i}+(5+1)\mathbf{j}\\ &= -4\mathbf{i}+6\mathbf{j}\end{aligned}$
The resultant lies in the second quadrant.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-1)--(0,7) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-4,6) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-4,6)--(-4,0);
\path (-2,0) node[below]{$4$} (-4,3) node[left]{$6$};
\draw[black] (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=123.6901,radius=6mm];
\path (-1.5,0.8) node{$A$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{6}{4}\right)\\ A&\approx56.3099^{\circ}\\ \theta&=180^{\circ}-A\\ \theta&\approx124^{\circ}\end{align*}$
(b) Subtract corresponding components.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\underset{\sim}{b}-\underset{\sim}{a}\\ &=(-6-2)\mathbf{i}+(1-5)\mathbf{j}\\ &=-8\mathbf{i}-4\mathbf{j}\end{aligned}$
The resultant lies in the third quadrant.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-9,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-5)--(0,2) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-8,-4) node[below left]{$\underset{\sim}{b}-\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-8,-4)--(-8,0);
\path (-4,0) node[above]{$8$} (-8,-2) node[left]{$4$};
\draw[black] (-1.2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=206.5651,radius=7.2mm];
\path (-1.8,-0.6) node{$A$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{4}{8}\right)\\ A&\approx26.5651^{\circ}\\ \theta&=180^{\circ}+A\\ \theta&\approx207^{\circ}\end{align*}$

(a) The vector lies in the second quadrant, so $h>0$. Its reference angle is $180^{\circ}-150^{\circ}=30^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.5)--(0,3) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-4,2.3094) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-4,2.3094)--(-4,0);
\path (-2,0) node[below]{$8$} (-4,1.1547) node[left]{$h$};
\draw[black] (-1.3,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=150,radius=9.1mm];
\path (-2,0.6) node{$30^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\tan30^{\circ}&=\frac{h}{8}\\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}&=\frac{h}{8}\\ h&=\frac{8}{\sqrt{3}}\\ h&=\frac{8\sqrt{3}}{3}\end{align*}$
(b) The vector lies in the second quadrant, so $m<0$ and $m+6>0$. Its reference angle is $45^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[->,black] (-4,0)--(2,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.5)--(0,4) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(-3,3) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-3,3)--(-3,0);
\path (-1.5,0) node[below]{$-m$} (-3,1.5) node[left]{$m+6$};
\draw[black] (-1,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=135,radius=8mm];
\path (-1.7,0.7) node{$45^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\tan45^{\circ}&=\frac{m+6}{-m}\\ 1&=\frac{m+6}{-m}\\ -m&=m+6\\ -2m&=6\\ m&=-3\end{align*}$
For $m=-3$, the components are $-3$ and $3$, matching the required second-quadrant direction.

